{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41699756",
      "title": "Navigating Between Pages",
      "sourceHash": "603475638c594a352a17babcfafb9fe0e45f4173b3d0865338543b5b2a4d5064",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 1.493,
          "en": "Okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.493,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "Now that we got this second page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 5.91,
          "en": "it would of course also be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 5.91,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "if we could get to this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "in any other way than manually updating the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "because no one does that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 16.683,
          "en": "It would be nice to have a link to that second page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 20.67,
          "en": "And for that, on that starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.67,
          "end": 23.193,
          "en": "we could add a new paragraph here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 27.55,
          "en": "and then maybe add an anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 30.453,
          "en": "where we say About Us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 34.23,
          "en": "And here the address then could be /about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.23,
          "end": 35.853,
          "en": "to go to that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.67,
          "end": 42.18,
          "en": "With that done, indeed, we have that link here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.18,
          "end": 45.423,
          "en": "and if I click it, I'm taken to this About Us page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.41,
          "end": 49.29,
          "en": "But this approach now has a flaw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.29,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "It's not ideal, and you can see that there is a flaw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 56.583,
          "en": "if you take a look at this refresh icon up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "as I click About Us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "you will see that it briefly turns to a cross,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "which always is a sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "that a brand new page was downloaded from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 71.703,
          "en": "So, we left the current page and got a brand new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "The disadvantage with that is that we now no longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 78.24,
          "en": "have a single-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "as we normally do when working with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 84.72,
          "en": "Now, of course, to some extent that makes sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.72,
          "end": 87.21000000000001,
          "en": "because I mentioned that with NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.21000000000001,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "you would build full-stack applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.61,
          "en": "where the content is rendered on the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 94.2,
          "en": "and therefore it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.2,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "that it's no longer happening in the front-end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 97.92,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.92,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "But actually the great thing about NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 102.81,
          "en": "is that we get both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.81,
          "end": 105.96000000000001,
          "en": "When we visit a page for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.96000000000001,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "by, for example, manually entering the URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "then indeed it's rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 114.60300000000001,
          "en": "we get the finished page, and we're here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.89,
          "end": 118.11,
          "en": "But if we are on a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.11,
          "end": 121.73,
          "en": "and we then navigate around by clicking links, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.73,
          "end": 123.63,
          "en": "NextJS allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "to actually stay in a single-page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 131.703,
          "en": "and update the UI with help of client-side JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "Now, technically the content of the Next page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.81,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "will still be pre-rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 141.78,
          "en": "but it will then be updated on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.78,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "with client-side JavaScript code, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "And therefore you can get the best of both worlds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.82999999999998,
          "en": "a highly interactive, reactive client-side application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.82999999999998,
          "end": 153.36,
          "en": "once it's active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.36,
          "end": 155.4,
          "en": "but a finished page being served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.4,
          "end": 157.95,
          "en": "if you are visiting the page for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.95,
          "end": 160.773,
          "en": "so, if you did not navigate around on it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 164.64,
          "en": "However, at the moment, we're not getting this benefit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.64,
          "end": 167.79,
          "en": "With that link here, the page is always reloading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.79,
          "end": 171.15,
          "en": "and we're not in that single-page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.15,
          "end": 172.53,
          "en": "And the reason for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.53,
          "end": 175.98,
          "en": "is that we're using the regular anchor element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.98,
          "end": 178.02,
          "en": "That works, but it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 180.723,
          "en": "get us out of that single-page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.56,
          "end": 183.45,
          "en": "In order to stay in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 186.57,
          "en": "we have to use a special component called Link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 190.023,
          "en": "which we can import from next/link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 195.6,
          "en": "This is a component provided by the NextJS framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.6,
          "end": 198.42000000000002,
          "en": "which you should use instead of the anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.42000000000002,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "if you have some internal link as we have it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "So, if you have a link that leads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 205.653,
          "en": "to another page of your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 209.64,
          "en": "It then still takes the ref prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 211.74,
          "en": "and you could still also add other props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.74,
          "end": 214.2,
          "en": "like className and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.2,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "But now it is a component that will actually ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 220.263,
          "en": "that we stay in that single-page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.4,
          "end": 224.07,
          "en": "So, with that link component being used here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.07,
          "end": 226.77,
          "en": "if you now take a look at that refresh icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.77,
          "end": 230.91,
          "en": "as I click this link, you see it never changes to a cross.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.91,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "It always stays the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "which proves that we're not leaving the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "we're not loading a brand new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 239.1,
          "en": "Instead, behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.1,
          "end": 241.68,
          "en": "the content of the next page will still be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.68,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 244.86,
          "en": "but it'll then be sent to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.86,
          "end": 248.61,
          "en": "and there it'll be handled by client-side JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 250.863,
          "en": "to update what we see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}